1 _DSCR Another child of Nicolas and Marguerite Roeder was Elizabeth Roeder Baivier Liffering, who is also shown in the glass negatives. Nicolas Roeder was born on Dec. 10, 1811 in Belgium (in Europe) and died on July 22, 1890 in the Town of New Holstein
2 CONC , Calumet County. He is buried at St. Anna Cemetery. His wife was Marguerite Flies. It is claimed she was also born on Dec. 10, 1811 in Belgium. She died on Jan. 12, 1887 in the Town of New Holstein and is buried at St. Anna Cemetery, Town of New H
2 CONC olstein.
